  ('1118789309266721131', 'The Truth', 2019, 'Drama', 'Hirokazu Kore-eda, Éric Gautier, Nicolas Cambois', 'Hirokazu Kore-eda', 'Catherine Deneuve, Juliette Binoche, Ethan Hawke, Clémentine Grenier, Manon Clavel, Alain Libolt, Christian Crahay, Roger Van Hool', 'PG', 'Fabienne is a star; a star of French cinema. She reigns amongst men who love and admire her. When she publishes her memoirs, her daughter Lumir returns from New York to Paris with her husband and young child. The reunion between mother and daughter will quickly turn to confrontation: truths will be told, accounts settled, loves and resentments confessed.', 'Fabienne is a star; a star of French cinema. She reigns amongst men who love and admire her. When she publishes her memoirs, her daughter Lumir returns from New York to Paris with her husband and young child. The reunion between mother and daughter will quickly turn to confrontation: truths will be told, accounts settled, loves and resentments confessed.', 'https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w500/uU2GVQ2dkltwtwTi5uHkmKAnCcU.jpg', 'tmdb:movie:517468'),
